🎯 Practical 1 — COMPLETE COMMAND SHEET

These are the commands we've covered:

ipconfig

Purpose: View IP configuration.

ipconfig /all

Purpose: Detailed IP/network configuration.

ping 127.0.0.1

Purpose: Test connectivity to your own computer.

ping example.com

Purpose: Test connectivity to a domain.

nslookup example.com

Purpose: Query DNS information.

tracert example.com

Purpose: Trace the network route.

netstat

Purpose: View network connections/status.

netstat -ano

Purpose: View connections with process IDs.

systeminfo

Purpose: View Windows system information.

nmap 127.0.0.1

Purpose: Scan your own machine for TCP ports/services.

nmap -sn 127.0.0.1

Purpose: Host discovery/ping scan.
